  "skill_short_description": "End-to-end orchestration of bacterial genome reconstruction, from raw reads to a fully annotated, high-fidelity genomic sequence. This meta-skill integrates preflight (input validation), assembly, polishing, validation, and annotation into a strict evidence chain based on the nf-core/bacass paradigm. Use when the user wants to assemble, polish, validate, or annotate a bacterial genome \u2014 or when they ask \"is my bacterial genome ready?\". Builds on the upstream read-qc-trimming skill. Pairs with the bettamt-style ask-user stop point pattern from Betta-WGS-agent.",
